  "goodToKnow": "Schleudern means to hurl or fling: einen Stein schleudern, and to spin laundry: die Wäsche schleudern (die Schleuder is a spin dryer or sling). A skidding car schleudert or gerät ins Schleudern, which figuratively means to get into trouble. When the car itself moves, the perfect uses sein: Das Auto ist von der Straße geschleudert. Der Schleudersitz is an ejector seat, also a job where you can be fired at any moment. Der Schleuderpreis is a giveaway price."
